## Structure

```
src/
├── main.ts                  ← starts the server (and ORM connection, if any)
├── app.ts                   ← composition root — wires everything manually (no DI container)
├── config/env.ts            ← the only file that reads process.env
├── middlewares/              ← error handling, validation glue
├── shared/                   ← database/cache clients used by more than one module
├── domain/<module>/          ← entities + repository interfaces — pure business, zero dependencies
├── application/<module>/     ← use-cases + DTOs — orchestrates domain objects
└── infrastructure/<module>/  ← controllers, routes, persistence — all framework/I/O details
```

Dependency rule: `domain/` → nothing. `application/` → `domain/` only. `infrastructure/` → `application/` and `domain/`. The composition root (`app.ts`) wires everything.

